"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[42759],{42759:function(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"content":"\\n\\n<center>\\n<RestaurantCard\\n          cover=\\"/assets/snippets/location/475eebdc599bba72e51b23fb14be4a7c.jpg\\"\\n          title=\\"Four Seasons King Hotteok\\"\\n          cuisine=\\"Korean Street Food\\"\\n          address=\\"14, Geojejungang-ro 19-gil, Geoje-si, Gyeongsangnam-do\\"\\n          rating=3.0\\n          tags=\\"restaurant\\"\\n        />\\n</center>\\n\\n## Review\\n\\nWhile looking around the market early in the morning, we decided to have a quick and light lunch.  \\nAs we wandered around, a <mark>bunsik stall</mark> inside the market caught our eye, drawing an unusually large crowd with a long queue compared to other stalls.  \\nIn fact, it was a spot we had already looked up beforehand and planned to visit, but we hesitated briefly because the line was longer than expected and there didn\'t seem to be many dine-in seats inside.  \\nHowever, figuring that waiting in line would take less time than searching for a new restaurant, we joined the queue without hesitation.  \\n```adcard\\n```\\nPerhaps because the neighboring vendors often complain about the line blocking their storefronts, the owner meticulously managed the waiting line the entire time, which left quite an impression.  \\nStill, the market aisle was so narrow that forming a double line would completely block the passage, making it structurally inevitable to obscure the adjacent shop.  \\nWatching that situation unfold made me feel self-conscious and uneasy throughout the wait.  \\n\\nMost customers were getting takeout, and seeing them pack generous assortments of fried snacks convinced me that this place is indeed a popular local favorite.  \\nBecause the indoor dining space was so confined, it seemed like opting to eat inside might require waiting quite a bit longer.  \\n```adcard\\n```\\nWe kept our order simple with <mark>tteokbokki</mark> and <mark>fried snacks</mark>, and fortunately a table opened up inside so we were able to sit down and eat.  \\n\\nThe tteokbokki was a <mark>rice cake tteokbokki</mark> prepared without green onions, subtly refreshed with cabbage and served with plenty of broth like a soup-style tteokbokki.  \\nThe accompanying fried snacks were clean-tasting, crisp, and not overly greasy, which was very satisfying.  \\nWhile not an extraordinarily unique flavor, it was comfortably and straightforwardly delicious—a meal anyone could enjoy with ease.\\n## Pictures\\n<pictures>\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/475eebdc599bba72e51b23fb14be4a7c.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Four Seasons King Hotteok\\">\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/e2d3c886f121da40cf64f620668fcbb6.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Four Seasons King Hotteok\\">\\n</pictures>"}')}}]);